Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_dirwrite.c
Line: 1198
Function: TIFFWriteDirectorySec
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: Allocation size uses ndir * sizeof(TIFFDirEntry) without guarding against overflow of the multiplication or truncation to tmsize_t in _TIFFmallocExt(). On 32-bit builds, a large ndir can wrap the requested size, leading to an undersized allocation and subsequent out-of-bounds writes when the array of ndir directory entries is populated later in this function.

